 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "Great civilisations grew in the Americas before Europeans arrived:\n• Maya (southern Mexico, Guatemala): city-states with stone pyramids-temples (Tikal, Chichén Itzá); writing in glyphs, an accurate calendar, astronomy and mathematics with zero. Classic peak about AD 250–900, then many cities were abandoned.\n• Aztec (central Mexico): capital Tenochtitlan on a lake, founded about 1325; floating gardens (chinampas), a strong army, tribute from conquered peoples. Conquered by the Spaniard Hernán Cortés in 1521.\n• Inca (Andes, Peru): capital Cusco; an empire about 1438–1533 linked by stone roads; Machu Picchu; records kept on knotted strings (quipu). Conquered by Francisco Pizarro (1532–1533).\nCauses of decline: Spanish conquest with guns and horses, European diseases (smallpox) that killed millions, internal wars, and (for the Maya) drought and overpopulation.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {
   "a": 1325,
   "b": 1521
  },
  "problem": "How long did the Aztec capital Tenochtitlan exist before the Spanish conquest?",
  "steps": [
   "It was founded about {a} and conquered in {b}.",
   "{b} − {a} = {b - a} years."
  ],
  "answer": "about {b - a} years",
  "checks": []
 },
